---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---
<DocsLayout title="band cronjobs — Band Docs">
  <h1>band cronjobs</h1>

  <p>
    The <code>band cronjobs</code> command group manages scheduled recurring tasks. A
    cronjob is a saved <code>(cron expression, prompt)</code> pair attached to one
    worktree: the repo's default-branch worktree or any other. When the cron expression
    fires, Band sends the prompt to a chat pane in that worktree.
  </p>

  <h2>Worktree &amp; ID</h2>

  <p>
    Every cronjob lives under the ID of its worktree, which is the <strong>key</strong> the
    update, delete and trigger commands take. The cronjob itself has a generated string ID like
    <code>cj_1234567890</code>. Those commands take both the key and the ID.
  </p>

  <h2>List cronjobs</h2>

  <pre><code>band cronjobs list
band cronjobs list --worktree my-app-main     # filter by worktree</code></pre>

  <p>Example output:</p>

  <pre><code>ID              NAME         CRON         WORKTREE         AGENT   SESSION  STATE     LAST RUN
cj_1701400000   review-prs   0 9 * * *    my-app-main      -       -        enabled   completed
cj_1701400123   weekly-deps  0 0 * * 1    my-app-main      codex   -        enabled   completed
cj_1701400456   integration  0 */6 * * *  my-app-feat-ci   -       sess-42  disabled  -</code></pre>

  <h2>Create a cronjob</h2>

  <p>
    <code>--worktree</code>, <code>--name</code>, <code>--prompt</code> and <code>--cron</code>
    are required. <code>--repo</code> and <code>--scope</code> no longer exist and fail with a
    message saying a cronjob belongs to a worktree.
  </p>

  <pre><code>band cronjobs create \
  --worktree my-app-main \
  --name "review-prs" \
  --prompt "Review all open pull requests and post a summary" \
  --cron "0 9 * * *"

# Pinned to a coding agent session
band cronjobs create \
  --worktree my-app-feat-ci \
  --agent codex --session-id sess-42 \
  --name "ci-watch" \
  --prompt "Check CI status and report failures" \
  --cron "*/15 * * * *"</code></pre>

  <p>Options:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>--worktree &lt;id&gt;</code> — the worktree the job runs in (required).</li>
    <li><code>--name &lt;name&gt;</code> — human-readable name (required).</li>
    <li><code>--prompt &lt;text&gt;</code> — prompt sent to the agent (required).</li>
    <li><code>--cron &lt;expr&gt;</code> — 5-field cron expression (required).</li>
    <li><code>--agent &lt;id&gt;</code> — coding agent id from settings. The default agent runs without it.</li>
    <li><code>--session-id &lt;id&gt;</code> — agent session id. Each run goes to the chat with that session, or opens a new chat on it. A session that cannot be opened fails the run. Chat dispatch only.</li>
    <li><code>--via chat|terminal</code> — where a run goes.</li>
    <li><code>--disabled</code> — start the job disabled.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Common cron expressions</h3>

  <ul>
    <li><code>0 9 * * *</code> — Every day at 9:00 AM</li>
    <li><code>0 0 * * 1</code> — Every Monday at midnight</li>
    <li><code>0 */6 * * *</code> — Every 6 hours</li>
    <li><code>30 8 * * 1-5</code> — Weekdays at 8:30 AM</li>
    <li><code>0 0 1 * *</code> — First day of every month at midnight</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Update a cronjob</h2>

  <p>
    Both <code>key</code> (the worktree ID) and <code>id</code> are positional. Pass any of
    <code>--name</code>, <code>--prompt</code>, <code>--cron</code>, <code>--worktree</code>
    (moves the job), <code>--agent</code>, <code>--session-id</code>, <code>--clear-session</code>,
    <code>--enable</code> or <code>--disable</code>. <code>--enable</code> and
    <code>--disable</code> are mutually exclusive.
  </p>

  <pre><code>band cronjobs update my-app-main cj_1701400000 \
  --cron "30 8 * * 1-5" \
  --prompt "Review open PRs and check CI status"

band cronjobs update my-app-main cj_1701400000 --disable</code></pre>

  <h2>Delete a cronjob</h2>

  <p>Pending runs are cancelled and the schedule is removed. Both <code>key</code> and <code>id</code> are positional.</p>

  <pre><code>band cronjobs delete my-app-main cj_1701400123</code></pre>

  <h2>Trigger a cronjob</h2>

  <p>
    Manually fire a cronjob now, regardless of its schedule. This is the same as a normal
    cron tick — it sends the prompt to the job's chat pane (queued when that chat is mid-turn) and does
    not affect the next scheduled run.
  </p>

  <pre><code>band cronjobs trigger my-app-main cj_1701400000</code></pre>

  <h2>JSON output</h2>

  <pre><code>band cronjobs list --output json</code></pre>

  <pre><code set:html={`{
  "jobs": [
    {
      "id": "cj_1701400000",
      "worktreeId": "my-app-main",
      "agent": "codex",
      "sessionId": "sess-42",
      "name": "review-prs",
      "prompt": "Review all open pull requests and post a summary",
      "cronExpression": "0 9 * * *",
      "enabled": true,
      "lastRunStatus": "ok"
    }
  ]
}`}></code></pre>
</DocsLayout>
